<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">K'awiil Chan K'inich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 741–c. 761</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Ruler 4 of Dos Pilas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">K'awiil Chan K'inich was the fourth ruler of the Classic Maya kingdom of Dos Pilas in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, reigning from 741. He continued his predecessors' wars across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petexbatun">Petexbatún</a> region and is recorded on monuments at Dos Pilas and Aguateca. In 761 he was defeated and driven out, and the kingdom broke apart amid warfare that left Dos Pilas ringed by hastily built walls.</p></div>
